If there were no fragmentation products forming a correlation, we would have eqn. 4.3 become \(p_{N}=Re\langle(e^{in(\phi_{i}-\Psi+\Psi-\phi_{j})})=Re\langle(e^{in(\phi_{i}- \Psi)})Re\langle e^{in(\phi_{j}-\Psi)}\rangle=v_{n}^{i}v_{n}^{j}\), but since a jet signal is seen above that of the underlying flow, \(p_{n}=v_{n}^{i}v_{n}^{j}+c_{n}\), so the ansatz for the correlation function then becomes:

\[C_{n}(\Delta\phi)=A_{0}e^{-\frac{\Delta\phi^{2}}{2\sigma_{0}^{2}}}+A_{\pi}e^{ -\frac{(\Delta\phi-\pi)^{2}}{2\sigma_{\pi}^{2}}}+B[1+2v_{2}^{a}v_{2}^{t}\cos{(2 \Delta\phi)}] \tag{4.4}\]

